Vita: --vita-fast-envelopes=off|on|verify (platform/vita/runtime/fast_actors.hpp switch
"envelopes", with --vita-fast-mtx on). J3DMtxBuffer::calcWeightEnvelopeMtx read a joint inverse
bind matrix from the model data (twelve big-endian floats) and multiplied it by the joint animation
matrix once for every mix that uses the joint. Both matrices stay as they are for the whole call,
so on computes that product once per joint per call and keeps it: the same MTXConcat of the same
two matrices, then the same weighted sums in the same order, so the same envelopes bit for bit.
Verify stores the envelopes as before, sums them again from kept products and counts differences.

